For all other cases, we recursively call the Fibonacci function with arguments n-1 and n-2, and add the results together. This recursion continues until we reach one of the base cases, at which point the recursive calls unwind and the final Fibonacci number is computed.

Note that the Fibonacci function is not optimized for efficiency, as it recalculates the same Fibonacci numbers multiple times. For larger values of n, it may result in significant performance issues.

